      "writtenOn": "2017-05-04T01:24:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems to me that if we want to store metadata about a command (such as which sandbox we want to run it in), then it\u0027d be more machine-readable and less confusing if we make a new struct for it:\n\ntype sandboxableCommand struct {\n  Sandbox string\n  Command Command\n}\n\nI imagine we\u0027d make some factory methods for generating them, with names like \"sandboxedMakeCommand(...)\" in case the details of creating them change (such as they are here).",
