      "writtenOn": "2017-05-04T02:28:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s basically what this implements, except we pass the name as an argument instead of in the function name.\n\nI don\u0027t think this can actually be simplified much more beyond what it is -- we could use a struct here so that the arguments would be named, but that makes the args ...string more annoying.\n\nThe Sandbox argument is intended to be opaque here, since it\u0027s likely to be defined completely differently for Linux vs Darwin.\n\nThe path/args also shouldn\u0027t be defined elsewhere. In this case they\u0027re fairly static, but that\u0027s not the case for the other instances.",
